  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe propose a wavelet-inspired hierarchical coordinate descent (WHCD) algorithm that leverages multi-scale decomposition to systematically explore the optimization landscape. The key insight is that the optimal solution exhibits self-similar structures across scales, which can be captured by decomposing the function into orthogonal wavelets. Unlike the current periodic optimization, WHCD handles the imbalance by first identifying energy concentration patterns and then reconstructing them through adaptive thresholding. The bit-reversal permutation mutation counteracts local optima trap in the shift-invariant optimization regime, while the energy-based repair mechanism ensures feasibility.\n\nMathematical specification:\n1. Discretize domain [0,2] into n_points grid points with dx=2/n_points\n2. Represent h(x) = \u03a3 c_j \u03c8_j(x), where \u03c8_j(x) = [-1]^{bitrev(j)} \u03c8_{base}(x) for wavelets\n3. Objective: min max_lag \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n4. Constraints: \n   - Feasibility: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1, \u03a3h_i dx=1\n   - Wavelet coefficients: c_j \u2208 [-1,1]\n5. Orthogonality relation: \u03a3 c_j c_k \u03c8_j(x)\u03c8_k(x) dx = \u03b4_jk\n6. Change detection: max( (\u0394c_j)^2 ) < threshold for stability\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Parent validation:\n   - Initialize h if initial_h_values exists, else generate sparse wavelet basis\n   - Project to feasible set using L1-constrained logistic mapping\n   - Scale to satisfy integral constraint\n\n2. Wavelet initialization:\n   - Select Daubechies wavelet coefficients with adaptive length\n   - Apply bit-reversal permutation with dynamic seed for diversity\n   - Threshold small coefficients to avoid overfitting\n\n3. Hierarchical descent:\n   - Iterative coordinate ascent:\n     * Group adjacent coefficients with energy metric\n     * Select lag window \u03c9 = 2\u03c0/k_max based on Fourier spectrum\n     * Apply wavelet denoising of magnitude (c_j) using soft thresholding\n     * Back-calculate grid values via inverse discretization\n   - Dominant lag feature extraction:\n     Calculate autocorrelation peaks and identify critical k shifts\n     Rank shifts by |k|(1 - \u03b4(k))\n\n4. Mutation rules:\n   - Bit-reversal mutation: j -> j_rev during crossover\n   - Dynamic window mutation: expand contract search window based on gradient estimate\n   - Energy-flipping: invert sign of coefficients with stable wavelet patterns\n\n5. Feasibility maintenance:\n   - Use energy-preserving coordinate projection\n   - Repair using:\n     h_new = (1 + tanh(accumulated_error)) * volume_preservation\n   - Step: adjust to maintain integral constraint:\n     scaling_factor = (n_points/2.0) / (current_sum * dx)\n   - Validate and clip: h_new = clip(h_new, 0, 1)\n\n6. Acceptance criteria:\n   - Local improvement requires \u0394c_j > \u03f5 and autocorrelation reduction\n   - Global time budget: monitor wall clock during coordinate descent phases\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n1. Primary variants:\n   - Wavelet complexity: M_num \u2208 [3,5] Daubechies orders\n   - Mutation intensity: \u03c3 \u2208 [0.8,1.5] for bit-reversed coordinates\n   - Energy threshold: \u03b2 \u2208 [0.05,0.2] for coefficient pruning\n\n2. Condition-adaptive variants:\n   - Dynamic lag detection activates for high correlation dominance\n   - Hybridization with random restart triggers under premature convergence\n   - Energy distribution optimization activates for low Hamming-like distance\n\nComputational budget:\n- Base resolution: n_points <= 2000 (300s)\n- Memory profile: O(n_points) wavelet coefficients + O(n^2) correlation matrix\n- Time allocation:\n  - Spectral analysis: 10%\n  - Wavelet optimization: 60%\n  - Repair procedures: 20%\n  - Feasibility checks: 10%\n\nValidation and return contract:\n1. Feasibility:\n   - Always ensure 0<=h_i<=1 via L1-clipping projection\n   - Verify sum(h_i)*dx == 1 within tol=1e-6\n   - Check correlation computation uses mode=\"full\" with full spectrum\n\n2. Return parameters:\n   - h_values: numpy array of length n_points\n   - c5_bound: float\n   - n_points: int\n\n3. Early termination:\n   - If budget exceeds at iterations: 500, current solution fallback\n   - Null improvement threshold: 1e-5\n\n4. Energy monitoring:\n   - Compute time-domain energy metric: E = \u03a3|h_i - h_avg|^2\n   - Session failure triggered when E_i/E_prev < 0.95\n\n5. Repair fallback:\nif not feasible: revert to initial parent if wavelet decorrelation threshold exceeded",
